.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ngx-add 1  "ngx-add " 
.SH NAME
ngx\-add \- Create and enable a new site (asks for anything not given as a flag)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBngx\-add\fR [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-domain\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-alias\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-type\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-local\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-socket\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-in\fR] [\fB\-\-ssl\fR] [\fB\-\-cert\fR] [\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-email\fR] [\fB\-\-websocket\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-redirect\fR] [\fB\-\-staging\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-credentials\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-body\fR] [\fB\-\-hsts\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-canonical\fR] [\fB\-\-route\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create and enable a new site (asks for anything not given as a flag)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-domain\fR \fI<DOMAIN>\fR
Primary domain, e.g. app.example.com (with edit: the new domain)
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-alias\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Extra server name, repeatable: \-a www.example.com \-a example.org (with edit: replaces the list)
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-type\fR \fI<TYPE>\fR
Site type: proxy | static | php
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-local\fR \fI<PORT|HOST:PORT>\fR
Upstream for a proxy site: PORT (on 127.0.0.1) or HOST:PORT
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Document root for static / php sites (default /var/www/<domain>, created if missing)
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
php\-fpm socket for php sites (default: the one found in /run/php)
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-in\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
Public port (default 443 with SSL, 80 without)
.TP
\fB\-\-ssl\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
SSL: letsencrypt | existing | none
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Certificate (fullchain) path, with \-\-ssl existing
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Private key path, with \-\-ssl existing
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fI<EMAIL>\fR
Email for the Let\*(Aqs Encrypt account (asked once if none exists). Let\*(Aqs Encrypt no longer sends expiry emails: use `ngx check` to monitor
.TP
\fB\-\-websocket\fR
Proxy WebSocket upgrades
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-redirect\fR
Don\*(Aqt redirect HTTP (port 80) to HTTPS
.TP
\fB\-\-staging\fR
Use the Let\*(Aqs Encrypt staging server (for testing; certificates are not trusted)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\fR \fI<PLUGIN>\fR
Let\*(Aqs Encrypt with the DNS challenge through this certbot plugin (cloudflare, route53, digitalocean…): wildcards, no port 80 needed
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-credentials\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Credentials file for the DNS plugin (e.g. /root/.secrets/cloudflare.ini, mode 600)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-body\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Maximum upload (request body) size, e.g. 50m; `off` for nginx\*(Aqs default (1m)
.TP
\fB\-\-hsts\fR \fI<on|off>\fR
HSTS: tell browsers to always use HTTPS for this domain (on | off)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\fR \fI<on|off>\fR
Password\-protect the site (users: `ngx auth add <site> <user>`) (on | off)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\-limit\fR \fI<RATE>\fR
Limit requests per client, e.g. 10r/s or 300r/m; `off` to remove
.TP
\fB\-\-canonical\fR \fI<on|off>\fR
Redirect the aliases (e.g. www.) to the main domain (on | off)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-route\fR \fI<PATH=PORT>\fR
Proxy a path to another local app, repeatable: \-\-route /api=8080 \-\-route /ws=10.0.0.5:9000 (with edit: replaces the list; `\-\-route off` removes all)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
No prompts: use flags, and current values / defaults for the rest
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show the config and what would change without touching anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  sudo ngx add                                    interactive
  sudo ngx add \-y \-d app.example.com \-l 3000      proxy to :3000 + Let\*(Aqs Encrypt
  sudo ngx add \-y \-d app.example.com \-l 3000 \-\-websocket \-\-email me@example.com
  sudo ngx add \-y \-d docs.example.com \-\-root /var/www/docs \-\-ssl none  static, HTTP only
  sudo ngx add \-y \-d blog.example.com \-t php \-\-root /var/www/blog
  ngx add \-y \-d app.example.com \-l 3000 \-\-dry\-run  preview only
